{{!
    @template tool_vae/backup_page

    The page "Sauvegarder dans Moodle", between its header or heading and the footer: a notification and, for a dossier with
    no declaration, the way back to it; or what a backup is, above the confirmation of the core that the page draws itself.

    Every text comes from the context, already worded by tool_vae\output\backup_page. The template holds no logic: the
    states exclude one another before. Every text is escaped (double braces), except two keys of HTML made by the core
    (triple braces): noticehtml, a notification ($output->notification()); continuehtml, the button that goes back to the
    dossier ($output->continue_button()).

    Classes required for JS:
    * none

    Data attributes required for JS:
    * none

    Context variables required for this template:
    * noticehtml - false, or HTML: the notification drawn instead of the sentence
    * intro - false, or a string: what a backup is
    * continuehtml - false, or HTML: the way back to the dossier

    Example context (json):
    {
        "noticehtml": false,
        "intro": "A copy of the dossier is saved in your private files, to be reimported later.",
        "continuehtml": false
    }
}}
{{#noticehtml}}
{{{noticehtml}}}
{{/noticehtml}}
{{#intro}}
<p>{{intro}}</p>
{{/intro}}
{{#continuehtml}}
{{{continuehtml}}}
{{/continuehtml}}
